.TH SHB-TRUST 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb-trust \- Manage explicitly trusted agents, tools, and processes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb trust <list|add|remove> [name]\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Configure authorized tools, MCP servers, and processes that have human-level trust boundaries.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBadd\fR
Authorizes a specific tool, executable, or MCP server to run with trusted boundaries.
.TP
\fBlist\fR
Lists all processes and tools currently recognized as trusted in the project policy.
.TP
\fBremove\fR
Revokes trusted status from an agent or process.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
$ \fBshb trust list\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb trust add git\fR
.TP
$ \fBshb trust remove git\fR
.SH SEE ALSO
shb(1)
.SH WEBSITE
https://secretharbor.dev
